Nathan: 

The biggest transition I’m trying to navigate right now is transitioning from a world tube model— which, I think inheritance mistakes from the way four dimensionality was imagined 100 years ago… Or at least the way later thinkers portray it. See, the direction that Time is moving is outwards. It’s not linear. It’s a spherical growth vector. All 4 dimensions are identical, except for the fact that they are growing at slightly different speeds… The three spatial dimensions we think of as space, are growing at a rate of H_0 while the (equally) spatial dimension we think of as time is growing at H_0 + c …light and neutrinos rise the faster one, hence spherical emission at c , while matter rides (or perhaps retards) the other three. There’s a slight precession, I think, and that’s what leads to all this super helical structure. Or something like that.

